{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111898","id":2935200302,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6u85ou","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111898","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111898.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111898.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111898","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111898/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111898/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111898/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/001c8c9c24dc5bce94d2fec8d7fdf378947d691a","number":111898,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Improve `Environment` saturation color adjustment.","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Closes godotengine/godot-proposals#13195 (the remaining item relating to saturation)\r\n\r\nThis commit changes the saturation color adjustment to behave as follows for all rendering configurations:\r\n\r\n- Apply saturation with luminance weights on linear-encoded values, preventing brightness from changing with certain colors.\r\n- Apply contrast after saturation to avoid a performance regression when HDR 2D is disabled. This ordering is reversed compared to Godot 4.5 and earlier.\r\n\r\n# Rationale and screenshots\r\n\r\nRationale and screenshots for this PR can be found in godotengine/godot-proposals#13195.\r\n\r\n# Changes and improvements\r\n\r\n**Problem:** Low-luminance colours change in apparent brightness when saturation is changed. A prime example is deep blue colours which appear to brighten when saturation is decreased and darken when saturation is increased.\r\n\r\nThe solution to this problem is to simply apply saturation to linear-encoded values using CIE luminance weights for the Rec. BT.709 primaries that Godot uses:\r\n\r\n| Original | Even weights (Godot 4.5 HDR 2D enabled) | This PR (Rec. 709 luminance weights)\r\n| -- | -- | --\r\n| <img width=\"576\" height=\"324\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a04f116b-2458-4197-8f1b-1c981cfadf24\" /> | <img width=\"576\" height=\"324\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8bbf2fbe-7f68-4aaf-af09-9030eb1d6076\" /> | <img width=\"576\" height=\"324\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d0350846-e5c8-4da6-9307-4fd3f767a399\" />","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"miles